The az vm identity assign -g myResourceGroup -n myVm command assigns a system-assigned identity to the virtual machine.

The az identity create -g myResourceGroup -n myVmIdentity command creates a user-assigned identity, and az vm update -n myVM -g myResourceGroup --set identity.type='UserAssigned' sets an existing user-assigned identity to a virtual machine.

