An administrator confirming that a user is compromised indicates that an administrator selected Confirm user compromised in the Risky users report or used the riskyUsers API. It is included as a nonpremium sign-in risk detection type, which are included with Microsoft Entra ID P1 licenses. Leaked credentials and a suspicious API Traffic are both considered user risk detection types. Unknown devices are NOT considered as sign-in risks. Which risk is classified as a sign-in risk? -> an administrator confirming that a user is compromised

